{title: 552 - The Lord's My Shepherd}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #552 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 552}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Am]The Lord’s [Bb]my [Am]Shepherd, [C7]I’ll [Dm/A]not [C/G]want.
[Am/E]He [B7]makes [Dm]me down [C]to [F/C]lie
[F/C]In [C]pastures [C7]green; [F/C]He [Am/C]leadeth [C7/Bb]me
[Gm]The quiet [Dm/A]waters by.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Am]My soul [Bb]He [Am]doth restore [Dm/A]again.
[Am/E]And [B7]me [Em/B]to [Dm]walk [C]doth [F/C]make
[F/C]Within the [C7]paths of [F/C]righteousness,
[Gm]E'en for [Dm/A]His own [C/G]name's [Dm/A]sake.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Am]Yea, though [Bb]I walk [Am]in [C7]death's dark [Dm/A]vale,
[Am/E]Yet [B7]will [Em/B]I [Dm]fear [C]no [F/C]ill,
[F/C]For [C]Thou [F/C]art [C7]with me; [F/C]and [Am/C]Thy [C7/Bb]rod
[Gm]And staff [Dm/A]me [C/G]comfort [Dm/A]still.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Am]My table Thou [C7]hast furnished
[Am/E]In [B7]presence [Dm]of [C]my [F/C]foes;
[F/C]My [C]head [F/C]Thou [C7]dost with [F/C]oil [Am/C]anoint,
[Gm]And my [Dm/A]cup [C/G]overflows.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Am]Goodness [Bb]and [Am]mercy [C7]all [Dm/A]my [C/G]life
[Am/E]Shall [B7]surely [Dm]follow [F/C]me;
[F/C]And [C]in [F/C]God's [C7]house forevermore
[Gm]My dwelling [C/G]place shall [Dm/A]be.
{end_of_verse}
